<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Montjuïc (1641)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1641">1641</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reapers-war">Reapers' War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Montjuïc was fought on 26 January 1641 on the hill of Montjuïc above <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barcelona">Barcelona</a>. Catalan militia and French troops repulsed the royal army of Philip IV under the Marquis of Los Vélez, which had advanced on the city. The victory saved Barcelona and the Catalan revolt, which had just placed Catalonia under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xiii-of-france">Louis XIII of France</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-montjuic-1641.jpg" alt="Battle of Montjuïc (1641)" width="320" height="220" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pandolfo Reschi · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Batalla_de_Montju%C3%AFc_de_1641.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In the civil war of 1462–1472 the Generalitat raised armies against John II, and in the Reapers’ War Catalan and French troops defeated a royal army at the <b>Battle of Montjuïc</b> in January 1641.</blockquote><a href="/empire/principality-of-catalonia">Principality of Catalonia · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>Days later Catalan and French troops defeated the royal army at <b>Montjuïc</b>. Claris died in February, and Catalonia returned to Philip IV's rule in 1652, losing Roussillon to France in 1659.</blockquote><a href="/state/catalan-republic-1641">Catalan Republic (1641)</a></li></ul></section>
